# The language file is a CSV that goes out to translators and comes back through a
# spreadsheet, and both LibreOffice and Google Sheets always write CRLF.
#
# #8's re-import safeguard is "diff the other columns and reject any change". That only
# reads if line endings are normalised first -- otherwise a returned file diffs as every
# line changed, and the handful of real changes are buried in it.
#
# Measured on #20, same returned file with five mangled cells, autocrlf switched off to
# stand in for a Linux CI runner:
#
#   with this rule:     6 changed lines  (the BOM, plus the five real ones)
#   without this rule:  54 changed lines (every line in the file)
#
# It was working already via core.autocrlf=true -- but that is set at machine level on
# the owner's Windows install, not in this repo, so nothing carries it to a fresh clone
# or to CI. This line does.
*.csv text eol=lf
